ogress shots... I&#039;m pretty sure I will go with jasmines (plus their website and Facebook have tons of photos of dresses they made) \n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1846954,"PostDate":1398644685,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>Icis, on 27 April 2014 - 10:09 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>I've ordered and received my second dress from Dressilyme, but that doesn't mean I stop looking at dresses! I often get frustrated that dressmakers don't provide pictures of their work even though they have made at least 5 of the same dress in the past. Anyways, I noticed there is an Etsy dressmaker that posts her actual work. Have a look and see what you think: <a href='https:\/\/www.etsy.com\/uk\/shop\/amazingbridalscom?ref=shopsection_shophome_leftnav' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>https:\/\/www.etsy.com...hophome_leftnav<\/a><\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nPlease share your photos! <br><br>\nYes, that's why I'm only choosing to go with dressmakers that show progress shots... I'm pretty sure I will go with jasmines (plus their website and Facebook have tons of photos of dresses they made) <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"kmkwedding2016@gmail.com","IpAddress":"70.72.195.234","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1390242208,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.