> Time: 1440130760 / Fri, 21 Aug 2015 04:19:20 +0000
> URL: /index.php?/REST/Forums/topic/getPosts?topicId=30824&start=6200&SessionId=3f98263b65d1a9d37c28ef2ea4e416c5
> User jacquewedding (283943)
Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.222.215.154","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4cf3f7190e27465ad453ec5dbbfd4929","RawContent":"I attached a picture of the dress I ordered and of the actual dress I got.\n\n\nBefore I ever even thought about doing this, I had tried on dresses at two different bridal stores. I was having a really hard time with how much money one dress could cost! And to even fathom doing a trash the dress after spending $1500-2000 on a dress!! Anyways, the dresses that I thought I would love ended up looking horrible on me, and then I found a dress that I really liked but wanted to make changes to which would have cost me even more!n\n\n\nThen I found this thread....I didn&#039;t even know that ordering from China was even a possibility! I searched and searched, and found this style which is almost identical to the dress I really liked but it had the sweetheart neckline which I really loved! When I first found this dress, it was on sale....but after thinking about it and looking at it multiple times a day, when I was finally ready to order, it was back to full price of over $600. I wasn&#039;t ready to pay that, so I thought my experience would end there....but I am persistent, and two weeks later it went on sale again! I ordered immediately! \n\n\nInput my order in on February 9, and chose the cheapest shipping method. My wedding isn&#039;t until October so I wasn&#039;t in any hurry. Amy at Dressilyme was in contact with me almost immediately. I had asked for pictures prior to sending and she said that they couldn&#039;t do that but to feel confident that it would be perfect. She also said that it would be 30-45 days to make and 10 days to ship. Fine with me. In February 26, I got confirmation that my dress was completed and had been shipped! And it arrived at my door on February 28!! Wow! \n\n\nI did order it custom to my measurements, which turned out amazing! The dress literally fits like a glove! The only part is that the corset back at the too comes almost together, but it think if I wear a bra or undergarment under it it will close into the v shape that a corset back should be. The original is in white, \n\nand I ordered mine in ivory. The color is perfect. The actually quality of the dress is amazing, just like any dress I tried on in a bridal store! Maybe a few stray threads here and there but that it easy enough to fix! \n\nThe lace on the dress is definitely different than that in the original, but it is very pretty. I think I like the lace in the picture better, but I am still happy with what I received. \n\n\nThe only alteration that really needs to be done is a bustle.\n\n\nAlso, I read somewhere that people dresses smelled funny...there is no smell on my dress at all! Lol\n\n\nOverall, I would definitely order from this site again! My bridesmaids are checking out dresses they might like and I will probably order them from here as well. \n\n\nFunniest part is that when my fianc\u00e9 and I spoke about wedding dress budget, he suggested it be $500, to which I laughed and laughed....but now who has the last laugh!? All in I paid $360 with custom sizing, shipping, and I had to pay another $20 when it arrived for customs. \n\n\nBest thing I did, now I can&#039;t wait to wear it on our we doing day!","Attachments":[{"Id":26853,"Name":"image.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_03_2014\/post-272291-0-34996800-1393869709.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_03_2014\/post-272291-0-34996800-1393869709_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200},{"Id":26852,"Name":"image.jpg","Url":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_03_2014\/post-272291-0-17285900-1393869641.jpg","ScaledUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_03_2014\/post-272291-0-17285900-1393869641_thumb.jpg","Width":900,"Height":1200}],"Id":1836435,"PostDate":1393856295,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I attached a picture of the dress I ordered and of the actual dress I got.<br><br>\nBefore I ever even thought about doing this, I had tried on dresses at two different bridal stores. I was having a really hard time with how much money one dress could cost! And to even fathom doing a trash the dress after spending $1500-2000 on a dress!! Anyways, the dresses that I thought I would love ended up looking horrible on me, and then I found a dress that I really liked but wanted to make changes to which would have cost me even more!n<br><br>\nThen I found this thread....I didn't even know that ordering from China was even a possibility! I searched and searched, and found this style which is almost identical to the dress I really liked but it had the sweetheart neckline which I really loved! When I first found this dress, it was on sale....but after thinking about it and looking at it multiple times a day, when I was finally ready to order, it was back to full price of over $600. I wasn't ready to pay that, so I thought my experience would end there....but I am persistent, and two weeks later it went on sale again! I ordered immediately! <br><br>\nInput my order in on February 9, and chose the cheapest shipping method. My wedding isn't until October so I wasn't in any hurry. Amy at Dressilyme was in contact with me almost immediately. I had asked for pictures prior to sending and she said that they couldn't do that but to feel confident that it would be perfect. She also said that it would be 30-45 days to make and 10 days to ship. Fine with me. In February 26, I got confirmation that my dress was completed and had been shipped! And it arrived at my door on February 28!! Wow! <br><br>\nI did order it custom to my measurements, which turned out amazing! The dress literally fits like a glove! The only part is that the corset back at the too comes almost together, but it think if I wear a bra or undergarment under it it will close into the v shape that a corset back should be. The original is in white, <br>\nand I ordered mine in ivory. The color is perfect. The actually quality of the dress is amazing, just like any dress I tried on in a bridal store! Maybe a few stray threads here and there but that it easy enough to fix! <br>\nThe lace on the dress is definitely different than that in the original, but it is very pretty. I think I like the lace in the picture better, but I am still happy with what I received. <br><br>\nThe only alteration that really needs to be done is a bustle.<br><br>\nAlso, I read somewhere that people dresses smelled funny...there is no smell on my dress at all! Lol<br><br>\nOverall, I would definitely order from this site again! My bridesmaids are checking out dresses they might like and I will probably order them from here as well. <br><br>\nFunniest part is that when my fianc\u00e9 and I spoke about wedding dress budget, he suggested it be $500, to which I laughed and laughed....but now who has the last laugh!? All in I paid $360 with custom sizing, shipping, and I had to pay another $20 when it arrived for customs. <br><br>\nBest thing I did, now I can't wait to wear it on our we doing day!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"candle_23@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"66.222.215.154","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1375747301,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-272291.jpg?_r=1388954341","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"candle23","Id":272291,"Name":"candle23","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"171.159.64.10","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7a7f2be21fee87ddf5bf4808e7a74ef5","RawContent":"is dressilyme like dhgate? there are different vendors? or is it like one vendor one feedback?\n[quote name=\"candle23\" post=\"1836435\" timestamp=\"1393870695\"]\nI attached a picture of the dress I ordered and of the actual dress I got.\n\nBefore I ever even thought about doing this, I had tried on dresses at two different bridal stores. I was having a really hard time with how much money one dress could cost! And to even fathom doing a trash the dress after spending $1500-2000 on a dress!! Anyways, the dresses that I thought I would love ended up looking horrible on me, and then I found a dress that I really liked but wanted to make changes to which would have cost me even more!n\n\nThen I found this thread....I didn&#039;t even know that ordering from China was even a possibility! I searched and searched, and found this style which is almost identical to the dress I really liked but it had the sweetheart neckline which I really loved! When I first found this dress, it was on sale....but after thinking about it and looking at it multiple times a day, when I was finally ready to order, it was back to full price of over $600. I wasn&#039;t ready to pay that, so I thought my experience would end there....but I am persistent, and two weeks later it went on sale again! I ordered immediately!\n\nInput my order in on February 9, and chose the cheapest shipping method. My wedding isn&#039;t until October so I wasn&#039;t in any hurry. Amy at Dressilyme was in contact with me almost immediately. I had asked for pictures prior to sending and she said that they couldn&#039;t do that but to feel confident that it would be perfect. She also said that it would be 30-45 days to make and 10 days to ship. Fine with me. In February 26, I got confirmation that my dress was completed and had been shipped! And it arrived at my door on February 28!! Wow!\n\nI did order it custom to my measurements, which turned out amazing! The dress literally fits like a glove! The only part is that the corset back at the too comes almost together, but it think if I wear a bra or undergarment under it it will close into the v shape that a corset back should be. The original is in white,\nand I ordered mine in ivory. The color is perfect. The actually quality of the dress is amazing, just like any dress I tried on in a bridal store! Maybe a few stray threads here and there but that it easy enough to fix!\nThe lace on the dress is definitely different than that in the original, but it is very pretty. I think I like the lace in the picture better, but I am still happy with what I received.\n\nThe only alteration that really needs to be done is a bustle.\n\nAlso, I read somewhere that people dresses smelled funny...there is no smell on my dress at all! Lol\n\nOverall, I would definitely order from this site again! My bridesmaids are checking out dresses they might like and I will probably order them from here as well.\n\nFunniest part is that when my fianc\u00e9 and I spoke about wedding dress budget, he suggested it be $500, to which I laughed and laughed....but now who has the last laugh!? All in I paid $360 with custom sizing, shipping, and I had to pay another $20 when it arrived for customs.\n\nBest thing I did, now I can&#039;t wait to wear it on our we doing day![\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1836686,"PostDate":1393957645,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>is dressilyme like dhgate? there are different vendors? or is it like one vendor one feedback?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>candle23, on 03 March 2014 - 02:18 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>I attached a picture of the dress I ordered and of the actual dress I got.<br><br>\nBefore I ever even thought about doing this, I had tried on dresses at two different bridal stores. I was having a really hard time with how much money one dress could cost! And to even fathom doing a trash the dress after spending $1500-2000 on a dress!! Anyways, the dresses that I thought I would love ended up looking horrible on me, and then I found a dress that I really liked but wanted to make changes to which would have cost me even more!n<br><br>\nThen I found this thread....I didn't even know that ordering from China was even a possibility! I searched and searched, and found this style which is almost identical to the dress I really liked but it had the sweetheart neckline which I really loved! When I first found this dress, it was on sale....but after thinking about it and looking at it multiple times a day, when I was finally ready to order, it was back to full price of over $600. I wasn't ready to pay that, so I thought my experience would end there....but I am persistent, and two weeks later it went on sale again! I ordered immediately!<br><br>\nInput my order in on February 9, and chose the cheapest shipping method. My wedding isn't until October so I wasn't in any hurry. Amy at Dressilyme was in contact with me almost immediately. I had asked for pictures prior to sending and she said that they couldn't do that but to feel confident that it would be perfect. She also said that it would be 30-45 days to make and 10 days to ship. Fine with me. In February 26, I got confirmation that my dress was completed and had been shipped! And it arrived at my door on February 28!! Wow!<br><br>\nI did order it custom to my measurements, which turned out amazing! The dress literally fits like a glove! The only part is that the corset back at the too comes almost together, but it think if I wear a bra or undergarment under it it will close into the v shape that a corset back should be. The original is in white,<br>\nand I ordered mine in ivory. The color is perfect. The actually quality of the dress is amazing, just like any dress I tried on in a bridal store! Maybe a few stray threads here and there but that it easy enough to fix!<br>\nThe lace on the dress is definitely different than that in the original, but it is very pretty. I think I like the lace in the picture better, but I am still happy with what I received.<br><br>\nThe only alteration that really needs to be done is a bustle.<br><br>\nAlso, I read somewhere that people dresses smelled funny...there is no smell on my dress at all! Lol<br><br>\nOverall, I would definitely order from this site again! My bridesmaids are checking out dresses they might like and I will probably order them from here as well.<br><br>\nFunniest part is that when my fianc\u00e9 and I spoke about wedding dress budget, he suggested it be $500, to which I laughed and laughed....but now who has the last laugh!? All in I paid $360 with custom sizing, shipping, and I had to pay another $20 when it arrived for customs.<br><br>\nBest thing I did, now I can't wait to wear it on our we doing day!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"cardenas.carla@gmail.com","IpAddress":"171.159.194.11","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1378978345,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":"none"},"FormattedName":"Carlicardenas","Id":273425,"Name":"Carlicardenas","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.222.215.154","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"8660114738d24d84896944b15d649114","RawContent":"They are just one vendor. You pretty much deal with one person through the whole process, they are very quick to respond...except it hPpens during the night since we are in different time zones!","Attachments":[],"Id":1836689,"PostDate":1393958037,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                They are just one vendor. You pretty much deal with one person through the whole process, they are very quick to respond...except it hPpens during the night since we are in different time zones!\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"candle_23@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"66.222.215.154","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1375747301,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-272291.jpg?_r=1388954341","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"candle23","Id":272291,"Name":"candle23","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.191.179.119","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"eff7e8b00a59d5a6d0e46bf53d09a43c","RawContent":"[quote name=\"candle23\" post=\"1836435\" timestamp=\"1393870695\"]\nI attached a picture of the dress I ordered and of the actual dress I got.\n\nBefore I ever even thought about doing this, I had tried on dresses at two different bridal stores. I was having a really hard time with how much money one dress could cost! And to even fathom doing a trash the dress after spending $1500-2000 on a dress!! Anyways, the dresses that I thought I would love ended up looking horrible on me, and then I found a dress that I really liked but wanted to make changes to which would have cost me even more!n\n\nThen I found this thread....I didn&#039;t even know that ordering from China was even a possibility! I searched and searched, and found this style which is almost identical to the dress I really liked but it had the sweetheart neckline which I really loved! When I first found this dress, it was on sale....but after thinking about it and looking at it multiple times a day, when I was finally ready to order, it was back to full price of over $600. I wasn&#039;t ready to pay that, so I thought my experience would end there....but I am persistent, and two weeks later it went on sale again! I ordered immediately!\n\nInput my order in on February 9, and chose the cheapest shipping method. My wedding isn&#039;t until October so I wasn&#039;t in any hurry. Amy at Dressilyme was in contact with me almost immediately. I had asked for pictures prior to sending and she said that they couldn&#039;t do that but to feel confident that it would be perfect. She also said that it would be 30-45 days to make and 10 days to ship. Fine with me. In February 26, I got confirmation that my dress was completed and had been shipped! And it arrived at my door on February 28!! Wow!\n\nI did order it custom to my measurements, which turned out amazing! The dress literally fits like a glove! The only part is that the corset back at the too comes almost together, but it think if I wear a bra or undergarment under it it will close into the v shape that a corset back should be. The original is in white,\nand I ordered mine in ivory. The color is perfect. The actually quality of the dress is amazing, just like any dress I tried on in a bridal store! Maybe a few stray threads here and there but that it easy enough to fix!\nThe lace on the dress is definitely different than that in the original, but it is very pretty. I think I like the lace in the picture better, but I am still happy with what I received.\n\nThe only alteration that really needs to be done is a bustle.\n\nAlso, I read somewhere that people dresses smelled funny...there is no smell on my dress at all! Lol\n\nOverall, I would definitely order from this site again! My bridesmaids are checking out dresses they might like and I will probably order them from here as well.\n\nFunniest part is that when my fianc\u00e9 and I spoke about wedding dress budget, he suggested it be $500, to which I laughed and laughed....but now who has the last laugh!? All in I paid $360 with custom sizing, shipping, and I had to pay another $20 when it arrived for customs.\n\nBest thing I did, now I can&#039;t wait to wear it on our we doing day![\/quote]\n\nGlad to know you are happy with your dress. Is there a specific reason you picked Dressilyme instead of DHGate vendors?","Attachments":[],"Id":1836790,"PostDate":1394023494,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>candle23, on 03 March 2014 - 02:18 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>I attached a picture of the dress I ordered and of the actual dress I got.<br><br>\nBefore I ever even thought about doing this, I had tried on dresses at two different bridal stores. I was having a really hard time with how much money one dress could cost! And to even fathom doing a trash the dress after spending $1500-2000 on a dress!! Anyways, the dresses that I thought I would love ended up looking horrible on me, and then I found a dress that I really liked but wanted to make changes to which would have cost me even more!n<br><br>\nThen I found this thread....I didn't even know that ordering from China was even a possibility! I searched and searched, and found this style which is almost identical to the dress I really liked but it had the sweetheart neckline which I really loved! When I first found this dress, it was on sale....but after thinking about it and looking at it multiple times a day, when I was finally ready to order, it was back to full price of over $600. I wasn't ready to pay that, so I thought my experience would end there....but I am persistent, and two weeks later it went on sale again! I ordered immediately!<br><br>\nInput my order in on February 9, and chose the cheapest shipping method. My wedding isn't until October so I wasn't in any hurry. Amy at Dressilyme was in contact with me almost immediately. I had asked for pictures prior to sending and she said that they couldn't do that but to feel confident that it would be perfect. She also said that it would be 30-45 days to make and 10 days to ship. Fine with me. In February 26, I got confirmation that my dress was completed and had been shipped! And it arrived at my door on February 28!! Wow!<br><br>\nI did order it custom to my measurements, which turned out amazing! The dress literally fits like a glove! The only part is that the corset back at the too comes almost together, but it think if I wear a bra or undergarment under it it will close into the v shape that a corset back should be. The original is in white,<br>\nand I ordered mine in ivory. The color is perfect. The actually quality of the dress is amazing, just like any dress I tried on in a bridal store! Maybe a few stray threads here and there but that it easy enough to fix!<br>\nThe lace on the dress is definitely different than that in the original, but it is very pretty. I think I like the lace in the picture better, but I am still happy with what I received.<br><br>\nThe only alteration that really needs to be done is a bustle.<br><br>\nAlso, I read somewhere that people dresses smelled funny...there is no smell on my dress at all! Lol<br><br>\nOverall, I would definitely order from this site again! My bridesmaids are checking out dresses they might like and I will probably order them from here as well.<br><br>\nFunniest part is that when my fianc\u00e9 and I spoke about wedding dress budget, he suggested it be $500, to which I laughed and laughed....but now who has the last laugh!? All in I paid $360 with custom sizing, shipping, and I had to pay another $20 when it arrived for customs.<br><br>\nBest thing I did, now I can't wait to wear it on our we doing day!<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Glad to know you are happy with your dress. Is there a specific reason you picked Dressilyme instead of DHGate vendors?<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mckiever.whetsel@gmail.com","IpAddress":"68.53.109.189","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1377357614,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-272881.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"mckievme","Id":272881,"Name":"mckievme","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"68.37.216.36","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"200fb57d768a81c69d4422314eeb90e2","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Great info!!! Wish I could see all the attachments :-( lol&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1836940,"PostDate":1394068675,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Great info!!! Wish I could see all the attachments :-( lol<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"latanyabryant@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.37.216.36","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1391296404,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-276443.jpg?_r=1391315507","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Tanya81","Id":276443,"Name":"Tanya81","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.222.215.154","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"6f1bff14d6322afc76e219f0561b974c","RawContent":"I just liked the idea of dealing with one vendor, dhgate kind of confused me because you had to find that perfect vendor who makes the best product and that just seemed like too much work for me! Lol","Attachments":[],"Id":1837073,"PostDate":1394137205,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                I just liked the idea of dealing with one vendor, dhgate kind of confused me because you had to find that perfect vendor who makes the best product and that just seemed like too much work for me! Lol\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"candle_23@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"66.222.215.154","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1375747301,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-272291.jpg?_r=1388954341","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"candle23","Id":272291,"Name":"candle23","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"66.191.179.119","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"958e5a691824af2e5b467c4adf536d30","RawContent":"[quote name=\"Tinkerbell82\" post=\"1835254\" timestamp=\"1393190335\"]\n[img]http:\/\/img.tapatalk.com\/d\/14\/02\/24\/ymyta7ez.jpg[\/img]\n\n[img]http:\/\/img.tapatalk.com\/d\/14\/02\/24\/ese5e2et.jpg[\/img]\n\n[img]http:\/\/img.tapatalk.com\/d\/14\/02\/24\/2avyzaga.jpg[\/img]\n\nHi ladies! Sorry it took so long- but here they are! Pics of my dress from babyonline. I need to get a crinoline (and some spanks lol) but this is it! Sorry for the bad pic quality. :)\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk[\/quote]\nWhat kind of crinoline will you be getting? Do you mind posting pictures after you purchase one with both the crinoline and dress on?\n\nI&#039;ve seen lots of brides say they need one, so I was just curious as to which ones brides were purchasing and how the crinoline changes the dress.","Attachments":[],"Id":1837181,"PostDate":1394203916,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>Tinkerbell82, on 23 February 2014 - 05:18 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/img.tapatalk.com\/d\/14\/02\/24\/ymyta7ez.jpg\" alt=\"ymyta7ez.jpg\"><\/span><br><br><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/img.tapatalk.com\/d\/14\/02\/24\/ese5e2et.jpg\" alt=\"ese5e2et.jpg\"><\/span><br><br><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' src=\"http:\/\/img.tapatalk.com\/d\/14\/02\/24\/2avyzaga.jpg\" alt=\"2avyzaga.jpg\"><\/span><br><br>\nHi ladies! Sorry it took so long- but here they are! Pics of my dress from babyonline. I need to get a crinoline (and some spanks lol) but this is it! Sorry for the bad pic quality. <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>What kind of crinoline will you be getting? Do you mind posting pictures after you purchase one with both the crinoline and dress on?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I've seen lots of brides say they need one, so I was just curious as to which ones brides were purchasing and how the crinoline changes the dress.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mckiever.whetsel@gmail.com","IpAddress":"68.53.109.189","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1377357614,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-272881.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"mckievme","Id":272881,"Name":"mckievme","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"67.78.194.58","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"5dc1c19443b1e8435d0482ebb7d30850","RawContent":"[quote name=\"mckievme\" post=\"1837181\" timestamp=\"1394218316\"]\nWhat kind of crinoline will you be getting? Do you mind posting pictures after you purchase one with both the crinoline and dress on?\n\nI&#039;ve seen lots of brides say they need one, so I was just curious as to which ones brides were purchasing and how the crinoline changes the dress.[\/quote]Actually, I decided against it.  Once I tried the dress on at the alteration shop with the shoes and everything, I prefered the way it flows vs. having a poofy skirt.  They did send me a cheap hoop one, but I never even bothered to put it on since I was happy with the way it was (plus it was one less decision to make). :)","Attachments":[],"Id":1837183,"PostDate":1394204306,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>mckievme, on 07 March 2014 - 02:51 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'>\n<div>\n<p>What kind of crinoline will you be getting? Do you mind posting pictures after you purchase one with both the crinoline and dress on?<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I've seen lots of brides say they need one, so I was just curious as to which ones brides were purchasing and how the crinoline changes the dress.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div><\/div>\n<p>Actually, I decided against it.\u00a0 Once I tried the dress on at the alteration shop with the shoes and everything, I prefered the way it flows vs. having a poofy skirt.\u00a0 They did send me a cheap hoop one, but I never even bothered to put it on since I was happy with the way it was (plus it was one less decision to make). <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"kristinacavanaugh@gmail.com","IpAddress":"204.87.40.1","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1369072692,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-269788.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Tinkerbell82","Id":269788,"Name":"Tinkerbell82","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"206.223.185.220","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c2f70d1b300eb2add4c669f82fd3d81c","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Just wondered if anyone has seen a site called dress day or day dress (something like that). It popped up last night while I was searching some things and I tossed it off, but realized afterwards that it was probably a site similar to these. Don&#039;t know if anyone has heard of, or dealt with them. If so, would be curious to know. They actually go by dress style numbers of designers, which really surprised me. One I was looking for popped up (that&#039;s how I found the site) and the price was unbelievable. But the old saying of what sounds too good to be true usually is keeps sticking in my head......&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1837196,"PostDate":1394208610,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Just wondered if anyone has seen a site called dress day or day dress (something like that). It popped up last night while I was searching some things and I tossed it off, but realized afterwards that it was probably a site similar to these. Don't know if anyone has heard of, or dealt with them. If so, would be curious to know. They actually go by dress style numbers of designers, which really surprised me. One I was looking for popped up (that's how I found the site) and the price was unbelievable. But the old saying of what sounds too good to be true usually is keeps sticking in my head......<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"achadwick9@yahoo.ca","IpAddress":"206.223.185.220","GroupId":38,"GroupName":"Moderators","JoinDate":1283444599,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-232000.jpg?_r=1434318164","PhotoWidth":570,"PhotoHeight":541,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"acw271011","Id":232000,"Name":"acw271011","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"74.138.102.75","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":30824,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"0862d789914fad48acb0ee5d1b5be7d8","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Hi everyone!&amp;nbsp;\n\nI was wondering if anyone had used Simply Bridal?\n\nThey are actually a US company and let you try dresses on at home for $19.95.\n\nI&#039;m considering ordering this one...\n\n&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.simplybridal.com\/shop\/wedding-dresses\/savannah-gown&#039;&gt;http:\/\/www.simplybridal.com\/shop\/wedding-dresses\/savannah-gown&lt;\/a&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;or this one\n\n&lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.simplybridal.com\/shop\/wedding-dresses\/ursula-gown&#039;&gt;http:\/\/www.simplybridal.com\/shop\/wedding-dresses\/ursula-gown&lt;\/a&gt;\n\n\nMost of their dresses are under $400&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1837601,"PostDate":1394498324,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Hi everyone!\u00a0<br>\nI was wondering if anyone had used Simply Bridal?<br>\nThey are actually a US company and let you try dresses on at home for $19.95.<br>\nI'm considering ordering this one...<br>\n<a href='http:\/\/www.simplybridal.com\/shop\/wedding-dresses\/savannah-gown' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/www.simplybri...s\/savannah-gown<\/a><\/p>\n<p>or this one<br>\n<a href='http:\/\/www.simplybridal.com\/shop\/wedding-dresses\/ursula-gown' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/www.simplybri...ses\/ursula-gown<\/a><br><br>\nMost of their dresses are under $400<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"rvalenka@gmail.com","IpAddress":"166.137.12.120","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1383890954,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-274900.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"rvalenka","Id":274900,"Name":"rvalenka","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":6402,"TotalPages":641,"CurrentPage":6200,"NextPage":6210,"PreviousPage":6190,"LastPage":6400},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
